.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt RAMFSD 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm ramfsd
.Nd RavenBSD in-memory writable filesystem server
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
registers the
.Dq ramfs:
scheme and serves a writable in-memory filesystem through the
.Xr open 2
protocol.
It supports regular files, directories and symbolic links.
.Pp
The default limits are 16 MiB of file data, 4096 inodes, 255-byte names and a path depth of 32
components.
File data beyond the limit is rejected with
.Er ENOSPC
before memory is grown.
Hard links are not supported and return
.Er EPERM .
.Pp
Unlinking an open file removes its name immediately and keeps the inode until the last open handle
closes.
Directories must be empty before
.Fn rmdir .
Rename replaces an existing file, or an empty directory of the same kind, and rejects moving a
directory into itself.
.Pp
A server-wide budget of 256 open-file descriptions applies; the next open returns
.Er EMFILE .
A duplicate shares the open-file description, its flags and its sequential cursor; the first close
does not remove the description, only the last close does.
The wire offset of
.Dv READ
and
.Dv WRITE
must be zero; a nonzero offset returns
.Er EINVAL .
.Pp
Directory reads are sequential.  A buffer smaller than the next packed entry returns
.Er EINVAL .
The server records the directory generation at the first read; a create, remove, rename or
symlink change in that directory invalidates the cursor and the next read returns
.Er EINVAL .
Reopen the directory to restart the listing.
.Pp
All content is lost when
.Nm
restarts; this is intentional for the first in-memory filesystem.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/ramfsd.toml
Service manifest.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr svcctl 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
